  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1030 PM MDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nLong wave UL trough covers roughly the western half of the CONUS\nwith a closed low over Eastern OR. Somewhere embedded in that\ntrough is the remnants of Rachel. Closer to home, a band of\nshowers and a few thunderstorms are moving through the CWA with\nactivity gradually waning and exiting, leaving most of us dry\novernight. The large-scale trough sticks around for Monday, but we\nlose any meaningful dynamics. Monday will be warm and breezy.\nMoisture, associated with Hurricane Simon, will be pulled\nnorthward thanks to the trough, and by Monday evening there will\nbe a low chance for showers/storms across Hudspeth County as most\nof any moisture associated with Simon stays east of the area. We\nwill see another, stronger wave of moisture on Tuesday, but again,\nmuch of the moisture will stay east, only giving Hudspeth County a\nchance for showers and storms. \n\nBy Wednesday the main UL low (same one that is now over Oregon)\nwill exit into the Plains, completely placing Southern NM and Far\nWest Texas in the dry slot, behind a Pacific front. This will\nbring seasonal temperatures for Wednesday and Thursday. \n\nThe aforementioned UL low will also send cooler air southward in \nits wake. The GFS is a tad quicker than Euro with the front, but\nin any case, winds will become gusty behind the front, especially\nfor West Slope areas beginning Thursday evening. Current operational\nNBM shows Wind Advisory and High Wind Warning level winds with \nthis front, so that will need to be closely monitored. GFS bufkit\nsoundings also very much supports this forecast with many of our\nwest slope locations showing a greater than 50% chance of\nexceeding 50 MPH gusts. Friday will be a much cooler day with \nhighs around 15 degrees below normal. It will feel a bit brisk! \n\nA piece of the trough breaks off on Thursday, and the GFS and \nEuro show a broad closed low forming off the Baja Coast by Friday \nwith moisture being drawn northward. This moisture is, checks and \nrechecks model data, associated with Simon, which manages to \nsurvive having part of it sheared off earlier in the week.",
